# Walker: towers on thin legs, a slab body with a red eye slit. Marches on towers.
grid 10
size 50 40 96
slot body Ink
slot trim Steel
slot eye Danger
# body slab high up
poly 70 86 body 5,8 45,4 48,20 45,36 5,32
box 10 12 86 40 28 90 trim
box 44 14 76 49 26 79 eye
# thin legs with knees
beam 15 10 72 10 4 40 2.2 body
beam 10 4 40 14 6 0 2 body
beam 15 30 72 10 36 40 2.2 body
beam 10 36 40 14 34 0 2 body
beam 35 10 72 42 6 38 2.2 body
beam 42 6 38 36 4 0 2 body
beam 35 30 72 42 34 38 2.2 body
beam 42 34 38 36 36 0 2 body
# feet
box 10 2 0 18 10 2 trim
box 10 30 0 18 38 2 trim
box 32 0 0 40 8 2 trim
box 32 32 0 40 40 2 trim
# R20 segments (a-34: the Walker slid rigid): four legs below the hips (z < 70), each turns about its hip under the
# slab; the body slab, hips and eye stay the root. Diagonal pairs swing together (+UnitGaits Walker).
part LegBL 4 0 0 24 15 70 14 10 70
part LegBR 4 25 0 24 40 70 14 30 70
part LegFL 26 0 0 48 15 70 36 10 70
part LegFR 26 25 0 48 40 70 36 30 70
